<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/martand-singh"><span class="enc-name">Martand Singh</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Martand Singh was the last ruling maharaja of Rewa in central India, succeeding his father in 1946.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/martand-sun-temple"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martand-sun-temple.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Martand Sun Temple</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Martand Sun Temple is a ruined Hindu temple dedicated to Surya on a plateau near Anantnag in the Kashmir valley.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/martanda-bhairava-thondaiman"><span class="enc-name">Martanda Bhairava Thondaiman</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Martanda Bhairava Thondaiman was Raja of Pudukkottai, a princely state in Tamil Nadu, from 1886 to 1928.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/martapura"><span class="enc-name">Martapura</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Martapura is a town in South Kalimantan, Indonesia, south-east of Banjarmasin on the Martapura river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/marthas-vineyard"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marthas-vineyard.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Martha's Vineyard</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Martha's Vineyard is an island off the south coast of Cape Cod in Massachusetts, the Wampanoag land of Noepe.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/marthanda-varma"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marthanda-varma.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Marthanda Varma</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Marthanda Varma was ruler of Venad from 1729 who built it into the kingdom of Travancore at the southern tip of India.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/marthinus-prinsloo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marthinus-prinsloo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Marthinus Prinsloo</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Marthinus Prinsloo was a frontier Boer leader in the Graaff-Reinet district of the Cape Colony.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/marthinus-wessel-pretorius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marthinus-wessel-pretorius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Marthinus Wessel Pretorius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Marthinus Wessel Pretorius was a Boer leader, the son of Andries Pretorius.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/martim-afonso-de-sousa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martim-afonso-de-sousa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Martim Afonso de Sousa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Martim Afonso de Sousa was a Portuguese nobleman and naval commander who led the first official colonising expedition to Brazil in 1530 to 1533.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-behaim"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martin-behaim.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Martin Behaim</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Martin Behaim was a Nuremberg merchant and cosmographer who spent much of his life in Portugal and the Azores.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/martin-bucer"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images